WEBVTT

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:11.970
Where you headed?

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.309
The Bridge.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.473
Mind if I walk with you?

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.482
Not at all.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:19.314
So, how's it going?

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.478
Not bad, I guess.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.216
Tuvok still giving you
a hard time?

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.848
No more than usual.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:25.983
I don't know about you,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.423
but when I think
about spending 70 years

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.429
on the same ship with that guy,
it gives me a headache.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.988
I get the impression a lot
of the crew agrees with me...

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.024
Maquis and Starfleet.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.998
Bridge.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.338
So what do you think?

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.672
About what?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.507
About what I've been saying...

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.911
that a lot of the crew
aren't too happy

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.539
with our Chief of Security,

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.676
and for that matter,
I don't think Captain Janeway

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:55.017
is winning any popularity
contests, either.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.818
Don't you agree?

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.950
Why do I get the feeling
that you're testing me?

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:03.053
Let's just say I'm interested
in your opinion.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.290
Why?

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.127
You're a good officer.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.634
I like you,

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.796
and I wouldn't want
to see you get hurt.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.635
Computer, halt turbolift.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.335
Look, what's this all about?

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.970
There are going to be
some changes around here.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.242
All of the Maquis are
in line, and about 25

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.112
of the Starfleet crew
are with us.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.617
Are you saying there's
going to be a mutiny?

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.988
And when the shooting starts...

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:32.150
I'm going to need to know
which side you're on.

00:03:34.011 --> 00:03:35.478
Well, Commander...

00:03:35.513 --> 00:03:36.673
Voyager's all yours.

00:03:36.714 --> 00:03:39.148
There's a first time
for everything, I guess.

00:03:39.183 --> 00:03:40.844
Don't worry, Captain,

00:03:40.885 --> 00:03:42.546
I'll keep your ship
safe and sound.

00:03:42.587 --> 00:03:43.554
I'm sure you will.

00:03:43.588 --> 00:03:45.488
Shuttle Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:03:45.523 --> 00:03:46.785
Go ahead, Mr. Paris.

00:03:46.824 --> 00:03:49.520
The shuttle's ready to go,
whenever you are.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.527
On my way.

00:03:50.561 --> 00:03:51.994
Captain, I've been thinking.

00:03:52.029 --> 00:03:53.087
Are you sure

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:55.098
you don't want to take
Lieutenant Tuvok with you,

00:03:55.132 --> 00:03:56.360
just in case the Rukani

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.698
turn out to be less friendly
than they seem?

00:03:58.736 --> 00:04:00.897
I assure you, Commander, I have
made thorough preparations

00:04:00.938 --> 00:04:03.406
for the Captain's safety
during her away mission.

00:04:03.441 --> 00:04:05.671
You, on the other hand,
are still adapting

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.371
to your duties as First Officer.

00:04:07.411 --> 00:04:09.902
Under the circumstances,
I believe my time will be

00:04:09.947 --> 00:04:11.107
better spent assisting you

00:04:11.148 --> 00:04:13.241
in your effort
to justify the trust the Captain

00:04:13.284 --> 00:04:14.376
has placed in you.

00:04:14.418 --> 00:04:16.352
I appreciate your concern
for my safety,

00:04:16.387 --> 00:04:19.083
Mr. Chakotay, but Tuvok's right.

00:04:19.123 --> 00:04:21.353
Lieutenant Paris and I
will be just fine.

00:04:21.392 --> 00:04:23.553
I'll see you in 24 hours.

00:04:25.563 --> 00:04:26.962
Lieutenant...

00:04:26.998 --> 00:04:29.967
I want you to keep close tabs
on the Captain's shuttle.

00:04:30.034 --> 00:04:32.730
Let's make sure she doesn't
run into any trouble.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.397
Aye, sir.

00:04:34.438 --> 00:04:37.464
Ensign, let's shut down
those transporters

00:04:37.508 --> 00:04:39.874
and start that diagnostic
we've been putting off.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.844
Sir, are you sure we shouldn't
wait for the Captain

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:42.846
to get back?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.405
Ensign Kim, you have been given
a direct order.

00:04:45.449 --> 00:04:47.940
Do as the Commander tells you.

00:04:47.985 --> 00:04:50.010
Aye, sir.

00:04:51.522 --> 00:04:54.616
Have you finished upgrading
the internal sensors, Ensign?

00:04:54.659 --> 00:04:56.684
I'm working on it, sir.

00:04:57.728 --> 00:04:58.752
I hope so.

00:05:05.803 --> 00:05:06.770
Wait here.

00:05:06.804 --> 00:05:07.930
Is something wrong, sir?

00:05:07.972 --> 00:05:10.805
No. It's just
tomorrow's duty roster.

00:05:17.615 --> 00:05:20.812
Sir, Captain Janeway's
shuttle has gone to warp.

00:05:20.851 --> 00:05:22.876
Thank you, Tuvok.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.945
Chakotay to all hands.

00:05:24.989 --> 00:05:26.081
Let's do it.

00:05:26.123 --> 00:05:26.987
Sir?

00:05:31.328 --> 00:05:32.920
Red Alert!

00:05:32.963 --> 00:05:34.794
Security to the Bridge!

00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:37.264
You're wasting your time, Harry.

00:05:37.301 --> 00:05:39.462
All my teams have taken control

00:05:39.503 --> 00:05:41.835
of Security, Engineering
and all key systems.

00:05:41.872 --> 00:05:42.964
You'll never get away with this.

00:05:43.007 --> 00:05:44.065
People will fight back.

00:05:44.108 --> 00:05:45.666
That's going to be
a little difficult.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.838
All your off-duty Starfleet
friends have been locked down,

00:05:48.879 --> 00:05:50.972
in quarters.

00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:04.217
I guess you've made your choice.

00:06:04.261 --> 00:06:05.489
Jonas to Chakotay.

00:06:05.529 --> 00:06:06.496
Go ahead.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.929
They're putting up a fight
on Deck 2.

00:06:08.032 --> 00:06:09.090
We could use some help.

00:06:09.133 --> 00:06:10.100
Carlson, O'Donnell...

00:06:10.134 --> 00:06:11.294
get these people to the brig.

00:06:11.335 --> 00:06:12.927
Ayala, take the conn and move us

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.938
out of com range
of Janeway's shuttle.

00:06:15.039 --> 00:06:16.028
You're with me.

00:06:23.814 --> 00:06:25.281
Deck 2.

00:06:25.316 --> 00:06:28.285
Thanks for watching
my back in there.

00:06:28.319 --> 00:06:30.787
Right.

00:06:30.821 --> 00:06:32.982
Are you okay?

00:06:34.325 --> 00:06:35.792
To tell you the truth, uh...

00:06:35.826 --> 00:06:38.226
shooting Harry...

00:06:38.262 --> 00:06:39.957
got me a little rattled.

00:06:39.997 --> 00:06:41.328
He's only stunned.

00:06:41.365 --> 00:06:43.094
We're not going
to kill anybody today,

00:06:43.134 --> 00:06:45.068
unless it's absolutely
necessary.

00:06:45.102 --> 00:06:47.002
Just stay close.

00:06:52.343 --> 00:06:53.833
Stay low.

00:06:56.213 --> 00:06:57.771
They've got us pinned down.

00:06:57.815 --> 00:07:00.409
We'll just have to shoot
our way past them.

00:07:00.451 --> 00:07:01.941
Ready?

00:07:08.659 --> 00:07:10.650
Seska!

00:07:10.694 --> 00:07:12.321
It's just like old times,
isn't it?

00:07:12.363 --> 00:07:13.159
Thanks for the help.

00:07:13.197 --> 00:07:14.164
We've got to get moving.

00:07:14.198 --> 00:07:15.256
Some of Janeway's people

00:07:15.299 --> 00:07:18.359
are trying to set up a command
center in the Mess Hall.

00:07:26.577 --> 00:07:28.272
I wouldn't do that
if I were you.

00:07:28.312 --> 00:07:29.939
This phaser's set on wide beam.

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:31.709
I could take you all
in one shot.

00:07:31.749 --> 00:07:33.774
Everybody drop your weapons.

00:07:35.319 --> 00:07:36.286
You heard the man.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:37.344
Drop your weapons.

00:07:38.789 --> 00:07:41.758
Don't look so surprised,
Commander.

00:07:41.792 --> 00:07:44.226
I know a winner when I see one.

00:07:44.261 --> 00:07:45.250
I'm with you.

00:07:45.296 --> 00:07:46.763
Do you want me to shoot him?

00:07:48.132 --> 00:07:49.759
We're still going to need
a cook.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.131
Chakotay to Engineering.

00:07:51.168 --> 00:07:52.533
What's your status?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:54.197
Engineering is secure.

00:07:54.238 --> 00:07:56.468
Transporter Rooms 1 and 2,
status.

00:07:56.507 --> 00:07:58.771
Transporter Room 1
is under control.

00:07:58.809 --> 00:08:00.743
Transporter Room 2 is secure.

00:08:00.778 --> 00:08:01.904
Shuttle Bay, status.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:03.913
Shuttle Bay is secured,
Commander.

00:08:04.014 --> 00:08:06.244
I'll take care
of the prisoners here.

00:08:06.283 --> 00:08:07.614
You two get some help

00:08:07.651 --> 00:08:08.777
and start rounding
up the personnel

00:08:08.819 --> 00:08:10.081
that are still locked
down in quarters.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.644
Bring them to Cargo Bay 1.

00:08:11.689 --> 00:08:12.656
We did it.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:14.681
Just like old times.

00:08:20.965 --> 00:08:22.762
You did a good job today.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.767
Thanks.

00:08:23.801 --> 00:08:25.735
Just make sure you keep it up.

00:08:25.769 --> 00:08:27.634
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:27.671 --> 00:08:30.936
It means I'm not as easy
to win over as Chakotay.

00:08:30.975 --> 00:08:32.966
Come on! Let's go.

00:08:41.986 --> 00:08:43.977
Wait here.

00:08:47.524 --> 00:08:48.957
Seska, what's going on?

00:08:48.993 --> 00:08:49.960
Move it.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:51.960
Why are we being
treated like prisoners?

00:08:51.996 --> 00:08:53.327
No talking.

00:09:00.938 --> 00:09:03.566
Over there,
with the rest of them.

00:09:03.607 --> 00:09:04.835
What are you going
to do with us?

00:09:04.875 --> 00:09:05.842
I said no talking!

00:09:05.876 --> 00:09:07.571
Hey, hey, hey, take it easy.

00:09:07.611 --> 00:09:09.169
I told you it was a mistake

00:09:09.213 --> 00:09:11.374
letting Starfleet people
in on this.

00:09:11.415 --> 00:09:13.440
Now's not the time, Seska.

00:09:16.287 --> 00:09:18.255
Take a good look around you.

00:09:18.289 --> 00:09:21.258
You're under armed guard.

00:09:21.292 --> 00:09:24.750
You may also notice that your
senior officers aren't here.

00:09:24.795 --> 00:09:26.763
They're in the brig.

00:09:26.797 --> 00:09:28.355
They'll be put off the ship

00:09:28.399 --> 00:09:31.926
at the first habitable planet
we come to...

00:09:32.036 --> 00:09:33.765
all except Janeway and Paris...

00:09:33.804 --> 00:09:35.635
who will arrive
at their rendezvous coordinates

00:09:35.673 --> 00:09:38.699
to find
that Voyager's not there.

00:09:38.742 --> 00:09:41.472
In short,
I've taken control of the ship.

00:09:41.512 --> 00:09:42.945
I don't blame any of you

00:09:43.013 --> 00:09:45.038
for the mistakes
of your leaders.

00:09:45.082 --> 00:09:46.709
So I'm giving you a choice.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.617
You can be put off the ship
with your superiors,

00:09:49.653 --> 00:09:51.245
or you can do what Neelix

00:09:51.288 --> 00:09:53.347
and some of your
other crew members

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.517
have already done, and join me.

00:09:55.559 --> 00:09:57.891
If you do,
you'll be part of a crew

00:09:57.928 --> 00:10:00.897
that's going to do whatever
it takes to get us home

00:10:00.931 --> 00:10:02.796
as fast as possible.

00:10:02.833 --> 00:10:04.630
Under my command,

00:10:04.668 --> 00:10:07.159
we won't let almighty
Federation principles

00:10:07.204 --> 00:10:08.967
get in the way of opportunities,

00:10:09.073 --> 00:10:11.769
the way Janeway did
when she destroyed the Array

00:10:11.809 --> 00:10:13.572
that could've gotten us home.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:16.204
And we won't be wasting
precious time,

00:10:16.246 --> 00:10:19.306
stopping to investigate
every insignificant anomaly

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:20.977
that we come across.

00:10:21.018 --> 00:10:23.316
What we will do...

00:10:23.354 --> 00:10:26.187
is use any means necessary
to acquire technology

00:10:26.223 --> 00:10:27.986
that can shorten our journey.

00:10:28.025 --> 00:10:30.186
To hell
with Starfleet regulations.

00:10:32.696 --> 00:10:35.995
You have 15 minutes
to make up your minds.

00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:37.432
B'Elanna.

00:10:37.534 --> 00:10:39.126
What's going on here?

00:10:39.169 --> 00:10:40.534
Computer, freeze program.

00:10:40.571 --> 00:10:42.163
Are you in the habit
of just walking in

00:10:42.206 --> 00:10:43.605
on people's
private holodeck time?

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.870
Well, it's not as if I caught
you dancing the rumba

00:10:45.909 --> 00:10:47.342
with a naked Bolian.

00:10:47.378 --> 00:10:49.312
We had a lunch date, remember?

00:10:49.346 --> 00:10:51.246
Is it lunchtime already?

00:10:51.281 --> 00:10:53.112
I must've lost track
of the time.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:56.608
Well, I expected to find you
shooting pool at Sandrine's,

00:10:56.653 --> 00:10:59.281
not hanging out with Seska.

00:10:59.323 --> 00:11:01.450
What sort of program
is this, anyway?

00:11:01.492 --> 00:11:02.686
It's really something.

00:11:02.726 --> 00:11:05.126
I was doing a routine purge
of the database...

00:11:05.162 --> 00:11:07.687
you know, taking out old files
that were taking up space...

00:11:07.731 --> 00:11:08.857
and I found this holonovel.

00:11:08.899 --> 00:11:13.097
It's a kind of "what if" story,
all about a Maquis mutiny.

00:11:13.137 --> 00:11:16.402
It's completely
compelling... and believable.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.465
I guess it's because
it's all about us.

00:11:18.509 --> 00:11:20.477
Who wrote it?

00:11:20.511 --> 00:11:22.308
Now, that...

00:11:22.346 --> 00:11:24.337
is the big mystery.

00:11:28.752 --> 00:11:30.982
Whoever the author is,
has gone to a lot of trouble

00:11:31.088 --> 00:11:32.521
to keep his identity a secret.

00:11:32.556 --> 00:11:33.921
It's been encrypted.

00:11:33.957 --> 00:11:34.924
Why do you suppose someone

00:11:34.958 --> 00:11:36.258
would try so hard
to be anonymous?

00:11:36.391 --> 00:11:37.323
Well, think about it.

00:11:37.359 --> 00:11:38.690
Whoever plays this program

00:11:38.727 --> 00:11:41.252
takes on the role of a
Starfleet Security Officer

00:11:41.296 --> 00:11:42.888
who gets approached by Chakotay

00:11:42.931 --> 00:11:44.899
to help the Maquis
take over the ship.

00:11:44.933 --> 00:11:46.628
I mean, it's
pretty inflammatory.

00:11:46.668 --> 00:11:50.365
You think we should
tell the Captain?

00:11:50.405 --> 00:11:52.066
Probably.

00:11:53.708 --> 00:11:57.007
It would be pretty hard for us
to give her a full report,

00:11:57.078 --> 00:11:59.546
if we don't know
how the story ends.

00:11:59.581 --> 00:12:02.141
Excellent point.

00:12:02.183 --> 00:12:03.343
Great.
Can you reset it for me?

00:12:03.385 --> 00:12:05.353
You?! I was just getting
to the good part.

00:12:05.387 --> 00:12:06.649
Oh, come on, B'Elanna,
be a sport.

00:12:06.688 --> 00:12:08.781
I've got to be back on duty
in less than an hour.

00:12:08.823 --> 00:12:11.087
Besides, isn't half
the fun of a holonovel

00:12:11.126 --> 00:12:14.892
having someone
to talk it over with?

00:12:14.929 --> 00:12:15.953
All right.

00:12:15.997 --> 00:12:17.021
You owe me one.

00:12:25.807 --> 00:12:27.604
Where are you headed?

00:12:27.642 --> 00:12:28.609
The Bridge.

00:12:28.643 --> 00:12:30.474
Mind if I walk with you?

00:12:30.512 --> 00:12:32.412
I was kind of hoping you would.

00:12:32.447 --> 00:12:33.914
So how's it going?

00:12:33.948 --> 00:12:35.415
Couldn't be better.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.475
Tuvok still giving you
a hard time?

00:12:37.519 --> 00:12:38.986
Doesn't he always?

00:12:39.054 --> 00:12:41.147
I don't know about you,

00:12:41.189 --> 00:12:42.747
but when I think
about spending 70 years

00:12:42.791 --> 00:12:44.986
on the same ship with that guy,
it gives me a headache.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.086
Not to mention
an upset stomach.

00:12:50.899 --> 00:12:52.161
Bridge.

00:12:58.139 --> 00:13:01.108
I hear you're planning a mutiny.

00:13:03.111 --> 00:13:05.079
Computer, halt turbolift.

00:13:07.215 --> 00:13:09.877
Who told you that?

00:13:09.918 --> 00:13:11.647
Let's just say there are rumors.

00:13:13.021 --> 00:13:15.114
Yeah, well, don't believe
everything you hear.

00:13:15.156 --> 00:13:16.145
Of course not.

00:13:16.191 --> 00:13:18.159
I just wanted you to know

00:13:18.193 --> 00:13:20.252
that whatever happens,
I'm with you.

00:13:21.996 --> 00:13:23.987
Computer, resume turbolift.

00:13:26.034 --> 00:13:27.968
I'm serious.

00:13:28.002 --> 00:13:29.970
Just tell me
what you want me to do.

00:13:34.376 --> 00:13:36.640
All right, Ensign, here it is.

00:13:36.678 --> 00:13:39.977
As soon as the Captain
leaves to meet the Rukani,

00:13:40.014 --> 00:13:43.142
I want you to put all crew
quarters on lockdown.

00:13:43.184 --> 00:13:46.483
I'll ask you if you've finished
upgrading the internal sensors.

00:13:46.521 --> 00:13:50.355
If you say yes, I'll
know we're ready to go.

00:13:50.392 --> 00:13:52.519
I understand.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.925
I'm watching you.

00:13:53.962 --> 00:13:55.953
No tricks.

00:14:00.468 --> 00:14:02.834
We are entering
the Rukani sector, Commander.

00:14:02.871 --> 00:14:03.895
Inform the Captain.

00:14:03.938 --> 00:14:04.962
Aye, sir.

00:14:13.047 --> 00:14:15.311
Well, Commander...

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.317
Voyager's all yours.

00:14:16.351 --> 00:14:18.842
There's a first time
for everything, I guess.

00:14:18.887 --> 00:14:20.047
Don't worry, Captain.

00:14:20.088 --> 00:14:21.953
I'll keep your ship
safe and sound.

00:14:22.056 --> 00:14:23.216
I'm sure you will.

00:14:23.258 --> 00:14:24.953
Shuttle Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:14:25.059 --> 00:14:26.219
Go ahead, Mr. Paris.

00:14:26.261 --> 00:14:28.559
The shuttle's ready to go,
whenever you are.

00:14:28.596 --> 00:14:29.563
On my way.

00:14:29.597 --> 00:14:30.928
Captain, I've been thinking.

00:14:30.965 --> 00:14:32.262
Are you sure you don't want

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.961
to take Lieutenant Tuvok
with you,

00:14:34.002 --> 00:14:35.560
just in case the Rukani turn out

00:14:35.603 --> 00:14:36.831
to be less friendly
than they seem?

00:14:36.871 --> 00:14:38.805
I assure you, Commander,
I have made

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:40.535
thorough preparations
for the Captain's safety

00:14:40.575 --> 00:14:41.974
during her away mission.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.841
You, on the other hand,
are still adapting

00:14:43.878 --> 00:14:45.903
to your duties
as First Officer.

00:14:45.947 --> 00:14:47.972
Under the circumstances,
I believe my time

00:14:48.082 --> 00:14:50.073
will be better spent
assisting you in your effort

00:14:50.118 --> 00:14:52.416
to justify the trust
the Captain has placed in you.

00:14:52.454 --> 00:14:54.684
I appreciate your concern
for my safety, Mr. Chakotay,

00:14:54.722 --> 00:14:55.950
but Tuvok's right.

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.185
Lieutenant Paris and I
will be just fine.

00:14:58.226 --> 00:14:59.784
I'll see you in 24 hours.

00:15:00.995 --> 00:15:02.587
Lieutenant,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.622
I want you to keep close tabs
on the Captain's shuttle.

00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:08.363
Let's make sure she
doesn't run into any trouble.

00:15:08.403 --> 00:15:09.563
Aye, sir.

00:15:09.604 --> 00:15:12.767
Ensign, let's shut down
the transporters

00:15:12.807 --> 00:15:15.401
and start that diagnostic
we've been putting off.

00:15:15.443 --> 00:15:17.274
Sir, are you sure
we shouldn't wait

00:15:17.312 --> 00:15:18.779
for the Captain to get back?

00:15:18.813 --> 00:15:20.110
Ensign Kim,

00:15:20.148 --> 00:15:21.911
you have been given
a direct order.

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:23.941
Do as the Commander tells you.

00:15:23.985 --> 00:15:25.509
Aye, sir.

00:15:28.523 --> 00:15:30.423
Have you finished upgrading
the internal sensors?

00:15:30.458 --> 00:15:31.755
Yes, sir.

00:15:31.793 --> 00:15:33.192
I hope so.

00:15:36.931 --> 00:15:38.523
Wait here.

00:15:38.566 --> 00:15:40.500
Is anything wrong, sir?

00:15:40.535 --> 00:15:43.504
No. It's just
tomorrow's duty roster.

00:15:51.346 --> 00:15:53.280
The Captain's shuttle
has gone to warp.

00:15:53.314 --> 00:15:54.645
Thank you, Tuvok.

00:15:54.682 --> 00:15:56.582
Chakotay to all hands.

00:15:56.618 --> 00:15:57.949
Let's do it.

00:15:57.986 --> 00:15:58.884
Sir?

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.444
Tuvok, get down!

00:16:10.031 --> 00:16:12.397
I guess you've made your choice.

00:16:12.433 --> 00:16:14.924
It's not over yet, Chakotay.

00:16:15.003 --> 00:16:17.130
Take them all to the brig.

00:16:34.522 --> 00:16:37.514
Sir, we have to do something.

00:16:37.559 --> 00:16:39.322
What did you have in mind,
Ensign?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:40.952
Escape, retake the ship.

00:16:41.029 --> 00:16:42.860
We will indeed attempt to do so,

00:16:42.897 --> 00:16:44.296
when the time is right.

00:16:44.332 --> 00:16:47.165
What about trying it now?

00:16:47.201 --> 00:16:49.169
Such a foolhardy proposal

00:16:49.203 --> 00:16:51.933
suggests a lack
of proper training.

00:16:51.973 --> 00:16:53.964
Need I remind you
that we are confined

00:16:54.008 --> 00:16:55.976
behind an electrostatic
force field?

00:16:56.044 --> 00:16:58.535
We can't just sit
here and do nothing.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.309
We are hardly doing nothing.

00:17:00.348 --> 00:17:02.612
We are observing the enemy,
watching

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:05.210
for any discernible patterns
in their procedures,

00:17:05.253 --> 00:17:07.551
looking for any weakness
in their defenses.

00:17:07.589 --> 00:17:10.422
How long is this observing
business going to take?

00:17:10.458 --> 00:17:12.016
It's been over an hour already.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:13.288
I'm getting bored.

00:17:13.328 --> 00:17:15.853
I am not concerned with
your amusement, Ensign.

00:17:15.897 --> 00:17:18.889
We are in a crisis situation
and we will follow procedure

00:17:18.933 --> 00:17:20.833
and procedure dictates
that we wait

00:17:20.868 --> 00:17:23.359
for the right opportunity
to attempt an escape

00:17:23.404 --> 00:17:25.668
whether it takes
an hour or a week.

00:17:25.707 --> 00:17:26.674
A week?!

00:17:26.708 --> 00:17:28.369
Who wrote this stuff?

00:17:30.378 --> 00:17:31.936
Hold Kim and Tuvok here.

00:17:32.046 --> 00:17:34.674
Bring the rest of them
to Cargo Bay 1.

00:17:38.486 --> 00:17:40.010
Enjoy the wait.

00:17:43.591 --> 00:17:45.855
...and we won't be wasting
precious time

00:17:45.893 --> 00:17:47.224
stopping to investigate

00:17:47.261 --> 00:17:49.661
every insignificant anomaly
we come across.

00:17:49.697 --> 00:17:51.961
What we will do is use
any means necessary

00:17:52.033 --> 00:17:54.831
to acquire technology that
can shorten our journey.

00:17:54.869 --> 00:17:57.963
To hell
with Starfleet regulations.

00:17:58.072 --> 00:18:00.563
You have 15 minutes
to make up your minds.

00:18:00.608 --> 00:18:02.838
I don't need 15 minutes.

00:18:02.877 --> 00:18:06.210
I'm with you right now.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:10.683
So, by the time
I got around to joining

00:18:10.718 --> 00:18:12.049
Chakotay's little band
of rebels...

00:18:12.086 --> 00:18:13.053
Uh-huh.

00:18:13.087 --> 00:18:14.679
...he was so suspicious
of my motives

00:18:14.722 --> 00:18:17.520
that he assigned me to lubricate
the warp plasma manifolds.

00:18:17.558 --> 00:18:18.582
You should've tried

00:18:18.626 --> 00:18:20.253
going along with the mutiny
from the beginning.

00:18:20.294 --> 00:18:21.261
It's much more fun.

00:18:21.295 --> 00:18:23.058
Oh, believe me,
next time I will.

00:18:23.097 --> 00:18:24.621
I couldn't help overhearing.

00:18:24.666 --> 00:18:26.190
You two are talking
about the new holonovel.

00:18:28.569 --> 00:18:30.537
I tried sending
an encoded message

00:18:30.571 --> 00:18:31.663
to Captain Janeway's shuttle,

00:18:31.706 --> 00:18:33.640
to warn her about the mutiny,

00:18:33.675 --> 00:18:36.542
but Chakotay caught me,
phasered me,

00:18:36.577 --> 00:18:37.908
and the program reset.

00:18:37.945 --> 00:18:39.776
Next time, I'm going to pretend

00:18:39.814 --> 00:18:41.679
to go along
with the conspirators,

00:18:41.716 --> 00:18:43.513
and then stage a counterstrike.

00:18:43.551 --> 00:18:46.748
I thought we were going
to keep this our little secret.

00:18:46.788 --> 00:18:47.755
Don't look at me.

00:18:47.789 --> 00:18:48.847
I didn't tell him.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.653
I heard about it
from the Doctor.

00:18:50.692 --> 00:18:51.920
The Doctor?

00:18:51.959 --> 00:18:53.392
I may have let it slip

00:18:53.428 --> 00:18:55.623
while I was running
his weekly diagnostic.

00:18:55.663 --> 00:18:57.153
Oh, great.

00:18:57.198 --> 00:18:58.961
Who else knows about it?

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.126
Don't worry about me.

00:19:00.168 --> 00:19:01.635
My lips are sealed.

00:19:01.669 --> 00:19:03.637
So what's this Ayala tells
me about a new holonovel?

00:19:06.874 --> 00:19:08.899
Get in line, Harry.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:13.276
Lieutenant Paris's
Personal Log, Stardate 50953.4.

00:19:13.314 --> 00:19:15.043
I've decided to take
B'Elanna's advice

00:19:15.083 --> 00:19:16.573
and replay the holonovel,

00:19:16.617 --> 00:19:18.517
this time,
as a full-fledged member

00:19:18.553 --> 00:19:20.521
of Chakotay's team of mutineers.

00:19:20.555 --> 00:19:23.149
I hope it turns out
better than before.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:27.091
Where the hell are
those warp engines?

00:19:27.128 --> 00:19:28.322
They're still off-line.

00:19:28.362 --> 00:19:31.024
We can't seem to get the
dilithium matrix reinitialized.

00:19:31.065 --> 00:19:32.259
It's been two days.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:33.267
Don't worry.

00:19:33.301 --> 00:19:34.529
B'Elanna's on it.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.067
Run a full security sweep.

00:19:38.106 --> 00:19:40.097
Something tells me there's
more to this engine problem

00:19:40.141 --> 00:19:41.438
than a faulty dilithium matrix.

00:19:41.476 --> 00:19:44.278
You think we've got
a saboteur on board?

00:19:44.411 --> 00:19:47.938
There's a ship approaching,
bearing 216 mark 33.

00:19:48.015 --> 00:19:49.482
It's Janeway's shuttle.

00:19:49.516 --> 00:19:50.813
Open a channel.

00:19:54.621 --> 00:19:56.179
Hello, Kathryn.

00:19:56.223 --> 00:19:57.952
How did it go with the Rukani?

00:19:57.991 --> 00:19:59.959
You're out of uniform,
Commander.

00:19:59.993 --> 00:20:02.962
There have been a few changes
since you've been gone.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:05.225
So I've heard.

00:20:05.265 --> 00:20:07.893
You think I don't have
any friends left on Voyager?

00:20:07.934 --> 00:20:10.960
Apparently, you do,
but I'll find them.

00:20:11.038 --> 00:20:12.198
And then what?

00:20:12.239 --> 00:20:14.537
Will you kill them
or just put them off the ship?

00:20:15.575 --> 00:20:18.601
Nobody has to die here today.

00:20:18.645 --> 00:20:21.113
I thought you were
a man of your word, Chakotay.

00:20:21.148 --> 00:20:23.139
I guess I was mistaken.

00:20:23.183 --> 00:20:24.980
I'm sorry
it had to come to this,

00:20:25.085 --> 00:20:28.680
but the crew believes I can get
them home faster than you can.

00:20:28.722 --> 00:20:30.747
It's going to be
a little difficult

00:20:30.791 --> 00:20:32.656
without warp engines, isn't it?

00:20:32.693 --> 00:20:35.218
Our warp drive may be
temporarily off-line,

00:20:35.262 --> 00:20:37.992
but our weapon systems
are fully operational.

00:20:38.065 --> 00:20:39.589
They're powering phasers.

00:20:39.633 --> 00:20:41.430
Kathryn, don't try to be a hero.

00:20:41.468 --> 00:20:43.265
I've been reasonable so far.

00:20:43.303 --> 00:20:45.168
I'll allow you
to keep the shuttle.

00:20:45.205 --> 00:20:47.673
I'll even transport you
some extra provisions,

00:20:47.708 --> 00:20:50.939
but if you don't stand down,
I will destroy your shuttle.

00:20:50.977 --> 00:20:56.279
You've just threatened
the wrong woman, Chakotay.

00:20:58.819 --> 00:21:01.413
What does she think
she's going to accomplish?

00:21:01.455 --> 00:21:03.787
We can obliterate them
in one shot.

00:21:03.824 --> 00:21:05.416
Not till I give the order.

00:21:05.459 --> 00:21:06.756
Reopen a channel.

00:21:06.793 --> 00:21:10.058
I don't know how, but they've
disabled our shields.

00:21:10.097 --> 00:21:11.928
We're completely vulnerable.

00:21:11.965 --> 00:21:14.934
Target their warp core and fire.

00:21:20.974 --> 00:21:23.408
I always said
Janeway was a fool.

00:21:23.443 --> 00:21:25.536
Intruder alert on Deck 8.

00:21:25.579 --> 00:21:26.705
It's Paris and Janeway.

00:21:26.747 --> 00:21:29.147
Janeway's no fool.

00:21:29.182 --> 00:21:30.809
She tricked us
into destroying her shuttle,

00:21:30.851 --> 00:21:32.785
then transported over
while the shields were down!

00:21:32.819 --> 00:21:35.413
She's trying
to free the prisoners.

00:21:35.455 --> 00:21:36.820
You've got the Bridge.

00:21:36.857 --> 00:21:37.915
You're with me.

00:21:46.299 --> 00:21:48.164
Get away from that panel!

00:21:49.436 --> 00:21:50.403
Oh!

00:21:50.437 --> 00:21:51.426
Drop it.

00:22:01.615 --> 00:22:03.640
Computer, resume program.

00:22:03.683 --> 00:22:06.447
The holographic simulation
has ended.

00:22:06.486 --> 00:22:09.114
Well, start it up again,
right where it left off.

00:22:09.156 --> 00:22:11.147
Unable to comply.

00:22:11.191 --> 00:22:12.385
Why not?

00:22:12.426 --> 00:22:15.623
Additional narrative parameters
have not been programmed.

00:22:15.662 --> 00:22:18.096
Are you saying
there's no more story?

00:22:18.131 --> 00:22:19.621
Affirmative.

00:22:19.666 --> 00:22:23.124
This is someone's idea
of a practical joke, right?

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:25.070
Please rephrase the question.

00:22:34.347 --> 00:22:35.712
There.

00:22:35.749 --> 00:22:37.649
I've bypassed
the security override.

00:22:37.684 --> 00:22:38.878
Try it now.

00:22:38.919 --> 00:22:42.753
Computer, identify the author
of holographic program entitled

00:22:42.789 --> 00:22:44.120
"Insurrection Alpha."

00:22:44.157 --> 00:22:46.148
That information is classified.

00:22:46.193 --> 00:22:49.492
I've tried every decryption
protocol I can think of.

00:22:49.529 --> 00:22:51.190
Whoever wrote this is good.

00:22:51.231 --> 00:22:52.698
Not to mention sadistic.

00:22:52.732 --> 00:22:55.860
I can't believe we've been
left hanging like this.

00:22:55.902 --> 00:22:56.869
Any luck?

00:22:58.305 --> 00:22:59.329
Me, neither.

00:22:59.372 --> 00:23:02.034
I've discreetly
questioned everybody

00:23:02.075 --> 00:23:03.940
I thought I could trust.

00:23:03.977 --> 00:23:06.445
Either nobody knows,
or nobody's talking.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.540
Remember the good old days
when it was impossible

00:23:09.583 --> 00:23:11.983
to keep a secret
on a ship this small?

00:23:15.021 --> 00:23:17.546
Well, if that takes care
of our official agenda,

00:23:17.591 --> 00:23:20.719
there's another matter
I'd like to discuss.

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:24.890
Commander Chakotay informs me
there's a new holonovel

00:23:24.931 --> 00:23:27.729
that's become quite
popular among the crew.

00:23:27.767 --> 00:23:31.464
It's been accessed 47 times
by 33 different crew members.

00:23:31.505 --> 00:23:33.234
I don't suppose anyone here
is familiar

00:23:33.273 --> 00:23:34.672
with what we're talking about.

00:23:35.876 --> 00:23:38.071
Actually, uh, Captain,
I'm the one who found it

00:23:38.111 --> 00:23:39.476
on the auxiliary database.

00:23:39.513 --> 00:23:40.810
I've been running it, too.

00:23:42.282 --> 00:23:44.341
Anybody else?

00:23:50.056 --> 00:23:52.991
I understand that the author
of this little opus

00:23:53.026 --> 00:23:54.994
has chosen to remain anonymous...

00:23:55.061 --> 00:23:56.995
perhaps because
of the controversial nature

00:23:57.063 --> 00:23:58.997
of the story,
which depicts Commander Chakotay

00:23:59.065 --> 00:24:01.056
as the leader
of a Maquis mutiny.

00:24:01.101 --> 00:24:04.264
Well, now, that the cat's
out of the bag...

00:24:04.304 --> 00:24:06.864
I want each of you
to talk to your staff

00:24:06.907 --> 00:24:09.535
and find out
who our anonymous author is.

00:24:09.576 --> 00:24:11.669
That won't be necessary,
Captain.

00:24:11.711 --> 00:24:14.043
I am the author
of the program in question.

00:24:15.549 --> 00:24:16.880
You, Tuvok?

00:24:16.917 --> 00:24:19.715
I never knew
you had literary aspirations.

00:24:19.753 --> 00:24:21.380
Not to mention talent.

00:24:21.421 --> 00:24:22.581
What a story!

00:24:22.622 --> 00:24:24.954
I'm afraid there's been
a misunderstanding.

00:24:25.025 --> 00:24:26.822
The program is not a holonovel.

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:28.794
It is a tactical training
scenario.

00:24:28.828 --> 00:24:30.591
When you first
invited the Maquis

00:24:30.630 --> 00:24:31.892
to join our crew,

00:24:31.932 --> 00:24:34.765
I believed that mutiny was
a very real possibility.

00:24:34.801 --> 00:24:37.827
With that in mind, I began
to write a training program

00:24:37.871 --> 00:24:39.429
for junior security officers,

00:24:39.472 --> 00:24:41.702
to prepare them
for such an eventuality.

00:24:41.741 --> 00:24:43.208
But you never finished it.

00:24:43.243 --> 00:24:46.076
No. As the two crews
began to work together,

00:24:46.112 --> 00:24:48.239
I concluded that
the threat of an insurrection

00:24:48.281 --> 00:24:50.806
was increasingly unlikely.

00:24:50.850 --> 00:24:53.080
I realized the program itself
might exacerbate

00:24:53.119 --> 00:24:55.713
the very conflict
I sought to avoid.

00:24:55.755 --> 00:24:57.222
Therefore,
I deleted the scenario...

00:24:57.257 --> 00:24:58.747
or so I believed.

00:24:58.792 --> 00:25:01.454
Apparently, you didn't account
for B'Elanna's exceptional

00:25:01.494 --> 00:25:02.518
computer skills.

00:25:02.562 --> 00:25:04.587
Nor her somewhat
excessive curiosity.

00:25:04.631 --> 00:25:06.895
I apologize for my
carelessness, Captain.

00:25:06.933 --> 00:25:08.298
Forget your carelessness.

00:25:08.335 --> 00:25:10.200
What you should be
apologizing for

00:25:10.236 --> 00:25:12.363
is leaving us all
hanging by a thread.

00:25:12.405 --> 00:25:14.396
You've got to finish the story.

00:25:14.441 --> 00:25:16.932
On the contrary, Mr. Paris,
the program has the potential

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:18.409
to incite animosity
among the crew,

00:25:18.445 --> 00:25:19.912
and must be permanently deleted.

00:25:19.946 --> 00:25:21.641
I have no doubt
the Captain concurs.

00:25:22.949 --> 00:25:26.350
With all due respect, Mr. Tuvok,
loosen up.

00:25:26.386 --> 00:25:28.411
You may have intended

00:25:28.455 --> 00:25:30.889
this program to be
a tactical training tool,

00:25:30.924 --> 00:25:32.084
but it looks to me

00:25:32.125 --> 00:25:34.525
like it's turned into a bit
of harmless fun.

00:25:34.561 --> 00:25:36.290
As the Captain of this ship,
surely you must...

00:25:36.329 --> 00:25:37.956
I'm more than just a Captain.

00:25:38.031 --> 00:25:40.625
I'm the leader of a community,
and communities need

00:25:40.667 --> 00:25:42.635
entertainment, culture,
creative outlets.

00:25:42.669 --> 00:25:44.933
Since we're not exactly privy
to every new piece

00:25:44.971 --> 00:25:48.168
of music or holonovel
that's written back home,

00:25:48.208 --> 00:25:49.197
I think it's only natural

00:25:49.242 --> 00:25:50.766
that we should start
creating our own.

00:25:50.810 --> 00:25:53.108
Besides, Tuvok, if the crew
doesn't get an ending,

00:25:53.146 --> 00:25:54.807
you may have a real mutiny
on your hands.

00:25:56.149 --> 00:25:57.980
If Tuvok doesn't want
to finish the story,

00:25:58.084 --> 00:25:58.982
I volunteer.

00:25:59.085 --> 00:26:00.552
Oh?

00:26:00.587 --> 00:26:02.714
I've always wanted
to write a holonovel.

00:26:02.756 --> 00:26:04.815
I think I could make
it pretty exciting.

00:26:04.858 --> 00:26:06.325
Good.

00:26:06.359 --> 00:26:07.383
Then it's settled.

00:26:07.427 --> 00:26:09.691
I, for one, can't wait to see
if Captain Janeway

00:26:09.729 --> 00:26:12.357
manages to outwit
the conspirators.

00:26:28.648 --> 00:26:30.445
Well, if it isn't Mr. Anonymous.

00:26:30.483 --> 00:26:32.576
Come to check up
on your replacement?

00:26:32.619 --> 00:26:34.951
Since the Captain
insists on allowing you

00:26:35.021 --> 00:26:37.251
to proceed with this
frivolous exercise,

00:26:37.290 --> 00:26:38.780
I thought you might benefit

00:26:38.825 --> 00:26:40.952
from the original
probability studies

00:26:40.994 --> 00:26:43.394
I conducted before
beginning the scenario.

00:26:43.430 --> 00:26:44.522
Well, thanks, Tuvok,

00:26:44.564 --> 00:26:46.930
but I don't need
any probability studies.

00:26:46.966 --> 00:26:49.491
I'm just sort of making it up
as I go along.

00:26:49.536 --> 00:26:51.060
Indeed.

00:26:51.104 --> 00:26:54.699
I'd be curious to know
what you've "made up" thus far.

00:26:54.741 --> 00:26:57.209
Well, I was thinking...

00:26:57.243 --> 00:26:59.939
Paris and Janeway
retake the ship,

00:26:59.979 --> 00:27:02.209
and then she decides to execute
all the conspirators.

00:27:02.248 --> 00:27:05.081
That is an entirely implausible
plot development.

00:27:05.118 --> 00:27:07.052
Captain Janeway
would never behave

00:27:07.087 --> 00:27:08.679
in such an inhumane manner.

00:27:08.722 --> 00:27:11.452
This isn't real life, Tuvok,
it's fiction.

00:27:11.491 --> 00:27:13.550
Don't get so caught up
in logic.

00:27:13.593 --> 00:27:16.528
Logic is an integral part
of narrative structure.

00:27:16.563 --> 00:27:18.793
According to the
"Dictates of Poetics,"

00:27:18.832 --> 00:27:19.924
by T'Hain of Vulcan,

00:27:19.999 --> 00:27:22.490
a character's actions
must flow inexorably

00:27:22.535 --> 00:27:24.628
from his or her
established traits.

00:27:24.671 --> 00:27:26.935
Well, I don't know anything
about T'Hain,

00:27:27.040 --> 00:27:29.702
but I do know what makes
an interesting story,

00:27:29.743 --> 00:27:31.711
and that's
unexpected plot twists.

00:27:31.745 --> 00:27:33.440
If you think I will allow you

00:27:33.480 --> 00:27:34.777
to turn this program
into a parody,

00:27:34.814 --> 00:27:36.213
you are sorely mistaken.

00:27:36.249 --> 00:27:38.274
Are you saying that you're going
to finish it yourself?

00:27:38.318 --> 00:27:39.683
Artistic differences?

00:27:39.719 --> 00:27:42.347
I would hardly call
Mr. Paris's ideas...

00:27:42.388 --> 00:27:43.446
artistic.

00:27:43.490 --> 00:27:45.890
Apparently,
my instincts don't comply

00:27:45.925 --> 00:27:48.257
with the Vulcan
"Dictates of Poetics."

00:27:48.294 --> 00:27:49.556
Well, I've got
a couple of suggestions

00:27:49.596 --> 00:27:50.563
that might help.

00:27:50.597 --> 00:27:51.586
Now, up until now,

00:27:51.631 --> 00:27:53.496
the story's been
nothing but action,

00:27:53.533 --> 00:27:54.966
which is fine, but what it needs

00:27:55.034 --> 00:27:57.269
is a little heart,
a little emotion.

00:27:57.402 --> 00:27:58.630
We are not writing
a romance novel,

00:27:58.670 --> 00:28:00.297
- Lieutenant.
- "We"?

00:28:00.338 --> 00:28:02.306
I've decided that your efforts

00:28:02.340 --> 00:28:04.638
would benefit
from my collaboration.

00:28:04.676 --> 00:28:05.643
Oh, really?

00:28:05.677 --> 00:28:06.905
Listen, I don't care

00:28:06.945 --> 00:28:08.344
which one of you
is writing this thing,

00:28:08.380 --> 00:28:10.507
all I'm saying is that there
is room in every good story

00:28:10.548 --> 00:28:11.913
for a little bit of passion.

00:28:12.017 --> 00:28:14.508
You know,
maybe you're onto something.

00:28:14.552 --> 00:28:16.577
I could add a steamy love scene

00:28:16.621 --> 00:28:18.748
between the Starfleet
conn officer

00:28:18.790 --> 00:28:19.848
and the Maquis engineer.

00:28:19.891 --> 00:28:21.017
Oh, that's realistic.

00:28:21.059 --> 00:28:22.686
How about a fresh pot of coffee

00:28:22.727 --> 00:28:25.093
to keep those creative juices
flowing, huh?

00:28:25.130 --> 00:28:26.256
Thanks, Neelix.

00:28:26.298 --> 00:28:28.596
Uh, while I'm here...

00:28:28.633 --> 00:28:30.260
Uh, let me guess.

00:28:30.302 --> 00:28:32.634
You have a suggestion to make.

00:28:32.671 --> 00:28:33.660
Of course not.

00:28:33.705 --> 00:28:35.502
I would never presume
to interfere

00:28:35.540 --> 00:28:36.837
in the creative process.

00:28:36.875 --> 00:28:38.604
More of a comment, really.

00:28:38.643 --> 00:28:40.270
About the Neelix character...

00:28:40.312 --> 00:28:41.779
How surprising.

00:28:41.813 --> 00:28:43.474
He would never betray
the Captain

00:28:43.515 --> 00:28:45.107
the way he does in that story.

00:28:45.150 --> 00:28:47.846
No offense, Mr. Vulcan,
but I don't think

00:28:47.886 --> 00:28:49.547
you understand
my character very well.

00:28:49.587 --> 00:28:53.216
Tuvok, did you forget to follow
the "Dictates of Poetics"?

00:28:53.258 --> 00:28:56.352
Perhaps we should find
someplace quieter to work.

00:28:56.394 --> 00:28:58.589
Now, that's the first
intelligent suggestion

00:28:58.630 --> 00:28:59.824
I've heard all evening.

00:29:01.099 --> 00:29:02.589
I believe our first step
should be

00:29:02.634 --> 00:29:04.499
to create a carefully
constructed outline

00:29:04.536 --> 00:29:05.764
of the remaining chapters.

00:29:05.804 --> 00:29:06.793
I told you, Tuvok.

00:29:06.838 --> 00:29:08.465
I'm just making it up as I go.

00:29:08.506 --> 00:29:10.906
We cannot proceed without
a carefully constructed outline.

00:29:10.975 --> 00:29:13.034
There you go with
that "we" stuff again.

00:29:13.078 --> 00:29:15.239
I don't remember agreeing
to let you help me.

00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:18.738
Need I remind you that it was I
who first began the scenario.

00:29:18.783 --> 00:29:22.651
And you think I'm compromising
your creative vision?

00:29:22.687 --> 00:29:24.382
In so many words, yes.

00:29:24.422 --> 00:29:26.890
And it is my duty to insure
that ship security

00:29:26.925 --> 00:29:29.553
is not compromised
by your creative vision.

00:29:29.594 --> 00:29:31.255
You had your chance
to finish this story

00:29:31.296 --> 00:29:32.695
and you wanted to delete it.

00:29:32.731 --> 00:29:34.926
True, but since that is
no longer an option,

00:29:35.033 --> 00:29:36.660
I am now exercising
my prerogative

00:29:36.701 --> 00:29:38.328
as the original author.

00:29:38.370 --> 00:29:39.337
Look, Tuvok...

00:29:39.371 --> 00:29:42.033
for the last time,
I don't need any help.

00:29:47.078 --> 00:29:48.443
Ah, there you are.

00:29:48.480 --> 00:29:51.472
I have several brilliant ideas

00:29:51.516 --> 00:29:53.279
for upcoming chapters
of your holonovel,

00:29:53.318 --> 00:29:55.445
as well as a list of revisions
and dialogue changes

00:29:55.487 --> 00:29:57.717
that I believe will improve
the earlier installments.

00:29:57.756 --> 00:29:58.882
I don't believe this.

00:29:58.923 --> 00:30:00.220
No thanks are necessary.

00:30:00.258 --> 00:30:01.953
In addition, I'm prepared
to offer my expertise

00:30:02.026 --> 00:30:04.358
in the creation
of holographic mise-en-scène.

00:30:04.396 --> 00:30:06.887
Computer, override
the EMH program's

00:30:06.931 --> 00:30:09.263
autonomous controls,
and transfer him

00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:10.358
back to Sick Bay.

00:30:10.402 --> 00:30:11.528
Now, wait just a minute...

00:30:12.570 --> 00:30:13.628
Thanks, Tuvok.

00:30:13.671 --> 00:30:15.298
Now that I think about it...

00:30:15.340 --> 00:30:17.308
I'll take it from here.

00:30:17.342 --> 00:30:20.175
You may find that difficult,
since I'm the only one

00:30:20.211 --> 00:30:22.145
who can make additions
to the program.

00:30:25.517 --> 00:30:27.178
All right, Tuvok, you win.

00:30:27.218 --> 00:30:29.311
We'll finish the story together.

00:30:29.354 --> 00:30:32.289
That is a very rational
decision, Mr. Paris.

00:30:32.323 --> 00:30:35.258
Computer, reinitiate
the holographic program

00:30:35.293 --> 00:30:37.284
entitled "Insurrection Alpha."

00:30:37.328 --> 00:30:39.592
Security clearance:
Tuvok-four-seven-seven-four.

00:30:39.631 --> 00:30:41.428
The program
has been reinitiated.

00:30:41.466 --> 00:30:42.694
The first thing
we're going to change

00:30:42.734 --> 00:30:44.929
is that title.

00:30:44.969 --> 00:30:46.300
Reformat the holo-matrix

00:30:46.337 --> 00:30:48.931
for the addition of new
interactive algorithms.

00:30:48.973 --> 00:30:50.804
The holo-matrix
has been formatted.

00:30:50.842 --> 00:30:53.310
Reopen the narrative
parameters file.

00:30:56.781 --> 00:30:59.648
Captain, we just lost power
in both transporter rooms.

00:30:59.684 --> 00:31:00.810
The com went down,

00:31:00.852 --> 00:31:02.649
and the holodeck systems
are completely scrambled.

00:31:05.223 --> 00:31:06.781
What are we doing in the brig?

00:31:06.825 --> 00:31:07.951
I have no idea.

00:31:07.992 --> 00:31:10.222
We haven't given
the computer instructions

00:31:10.261 --> 00:31:11.626
to create a location yet.

00:31:11.663 --> 00:31:12.630
Hello, Tuvok.

00:31:12.664 --> 00:31:14.097
I've been expecting you.

00:31:15.099 --> 00:31:16.589
If you can see me,

00:31:16.634 --> 00:31:18.966
you've obviously reopened
the narrative parameters file

00:31:19.070 --> 00:31:21.595
of the tactical scenario
you've been working on.

00:31:21.639 --> 00:31:22.970
How do you know that?

00:31:23.041 --> 00:31:24.235
You're a hologram.

00:31:24.275 --> 00:31:25.333
That's right.

00:31:25.376 --> 00:31:27.810
A holographic representation
of Seska...

00:31:27.846 --> 00:31:30.280
one of the Maquis
shipmates you betrayed.

00:31:30.315 --> 00:31:32.283
I would've thought
all that time you spent

00:31:32.317 --> 00:31:34.979
spying on us might've given
you a little more insight

00:31:35.086 --> 00:31:37.281
into the Maquis,
but after looking over

00:31:37.322 --> 00:31:38.983
what you've already written,

00:31:39.090 --> 00:31:40.955
I can see you need
a little help.

00:31:40.992 --> 00:31:43.586
So I've created
this representation of myself

00:31:43.628 --> 00:31:46.290
to guide you through the rest
of the program.

00:31:46.331 --> 00:31:47.992
There is no more program.

00:31:48.066 --> 00:31:49.465
There is now.

00:31:50.635 --> 00:31:52.603
I finished writing it for you...

00:31:52.637 --> 00:31:54.571
with a few revisions of my own.

00:31:54.606 --> 00:31:55.573
Revisions?

00:31:55.607 --> 00:31:56.574
To start with,

00:31:56.608 --> 00:31:58.235
the holodeck is now sealed.

00:31:58.276 --> 00:31:59.800
Your friends will find it

00:31:59.844 --> 00:32:02.278
very difficult to get
you out of here.

00:32:02.313 --> 00:32:04.372
And the safety protocols
are off,

00:32:04.415 --> 00:32:06.747
which means, if I shoot you...

00:32:06.784 --> 00:32:08.581
and I am going to shoot you...

00:32:08.620 --> 00:32:09.917
you'll die.

00:32:11.289 --> 00:32:13.314
But not just yet.

00:32:18.396 --> 00:32:20.660
You've got ten seconds to run.

00:32:27.338 --> 00:32:29.169
Nine, eight...

00:32:29.207 --> 00:32:30.834
Computer, end program.

00:32:30.875 --> 00:32:32.934
...seven, six...

00:32:32.977 --> 00:32:33.966
Holodeck 1 to Bridge.

00:32:34.078 --> 00:32:35.238
...five...
Emergency transport.

00:32:35.280 --> 00:32:36.975
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

00:32:37.048 --> 00:32:39.141
The moment you restarted
the program,

00:32:39.183 --> 00:32:40.673
the com system went down.

00:32:40.718 --> 00:32:42.982
Four... three...

00:32:43.054 --> 00:32:44.544
I guess we better do
what she says.

00:32:44.589 --> 00:32:48.525
...two, one...

00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:50.994
You should never
have crossed her, Tuvok.

00:32:51.062 --> 00:32:53.223
"She" has been dead
for over a year now.

00:32:53.264 --> 00:32:55.198
There would've been no way to
predict this turn of events.

00:32:55.233 --> 00:32:56.723
I guess we should've known
Seska wouldn't let

00:32:56.768 --> 00:32:58.599
a little thing like death
stop her from getting even.

00:32:58.636 --> 00:33:01.230
Tuvok, Tom.

00:33:01.272 --> 00:33:02.899
In here.

00:33:02.941 --> 00:33:04.238
Captain.

00:33:04.275 --> 00:33:06.209
We're going to have
to transport to the Cargo Bay

00:33:06.244 --> 00:33:07.404
to free the rest
of the prisoners.

00:33:07.445 --> 00:33:09.003
It's safer than trying
to make it on foot.

00:33:11.115 --> 00:33:12.412
She's a hologram, too.

00:33:12.450 --> 00:33:14.281
Apparently, she believes
we're here

00:33:14.319 --> 00:33:16.116
to help her retake the ship
from the mutineers.

00:33:16.154 --> 00:33:18.520
I say we play along.

00:33:18.556 --> 00:33:20.547
We could use all the help
we can get against Seska.

00:33:20.592 --> 00:33:23.060
You're forgetting it was Seska
who rewrote the scenario.

00:33:23.094 --> 00:33:24.356
For all we know,
she's programmed

00:33:24.395 --> 00:33:25.362
Captain Janeway to betray us.

00:33:25.396 --> 00:33:26.863
I suppose you have
a better idea?

00:33:26.898 --> 00:33:28.525
The safest course

00:33:28.566 --> 00:33:31.091
of action is to avoid
participation of any kind.

00:33:31.135 --> 00:33:33.660
Eventually, the real Captain
will discover our predicament,

00:33:33.705 --> 00:33:35.468
and shut down the program
from the outside.

00:33:35.506 --> 00:33:37.531
Let's move.

00:33:37.575 --> 00:33:39.440
Hold it right there.

00:33:39.477 --> 00:33:41.377
Back off.

00:33:41.412 --> 00:33:42.811
Or what? You'll shoot us?

00:33:42.847 --> 00:33:43.814
Go right ahead.

00:33:43.848 --> 00:33:45.839
Whatever you say.

00:33:50.188 --> 00:33:52.122
Poor Kathryn.

00:33:52.156 --> 00:33:53.646
I guess nobody told her
the phaser rifles

00:33:53.691 --> 00:33:56.751
from Storage Locker 3
have been malfunctioning.

00:33:58.930 --> 00:34:01.091
You're an incredible woman,
Seska.

00:34:06.437 --> 00:34:08.905
You see who's in charge
now, don't you?

00:34:08.940 --> 00:34:11.500
So, if I were you,
I'd get moving again.

00:34:11.542 --> 00:34:12.941
The program's not over.

00:34:13.011 --> 00:34:14.911
We have no intention
of participating

00:34:14.946 --> 00:34:16.243
in this exercise.

00:34:16.280 --> 00:34:18.748
You don't want to end up
like your Captain, do you?

00:34:18.783 --> 00:34:21.251
You programmed all this...
the malfunctioning phaser,

00:34:21.285 --> 00:34:23.583
a version of Chakotay
who's attracted to you...

00:34:23.621 --> 00:34:24.679
None of it's real.

00:34:24.722 --> 00:34:25.950
You hear that?

00:34:26.057 --> 00:34:27.957
He thinks this is a game.

00:34:28.059 --> 00:34:29.822
Show him he's wrong.

00:34:29.861 --> 00:34:33.024
I've been waiting
a long time for this.

00:34:34.866 --> 00:34:35.833
Next time, you'll believe me

00:34:35.867 --> 00:34:38.358
when I tell you the safety
protocols are off.

00:34:38.403 --> 00:34:39.836
Now, you've got five seconds

00:34:39.871 --> 00:34:41.634
to start running again,
or you'll end up

00:34:41.673 --> 00:34:42.970
with more than a flesh wound.

00:34:46.477 --> 00:34:49.446
So much for not playing
along with Seska's program.

00:34:49.480 --> 00:34:50.572
Are you able to continue?

00:34:50.615 --> 00:34:51.707
I'll keep up.

00:34:51.749 --> 00:34:53.546
The question is:
Where are we going?

00:34:53.584 --> 00:34:54.812
I have an idea.

00:34:54.852 --> 00:34:55.876
What's the point?

00:34:55.920 --> 00:34:57.387
This isn't the real Sick Bay.

00:34:57.422 --> 00:34:58.821
I may be able to use
some of this

00:34:58.856 --> 00:35:00.687
holographic equipment
to treat your wound.

00:35:00.725 --> 00:35:03.057
Besides, it's as good a place
as any to hide from Seska.

00:35:03.094 --> 00:35:04.857
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:35:04.896 --> 00:35:06.693
No emergency, Doc.
I'm fine.

00:35:06.731 --> 00:35:08.562
Nonsense. You have
second-degree phaser burns.

00:35:08.599 --> 00:35:09.827
Please have a seat
on bio-bed one.

00:35:09.867 --> 00:35:11.061
That's all right, Doc.

00:35:11.102 --> 00:35:12.364
I'm telling you, I feel fine.

00:35:12.403 --> 00:35:14.064
You require treatment.

00:35:14.105 --> 00:35:15.231
20 cc's nitric acid.

00:35:16.274 --> 00:35:17.764
A little proverbial
salt in the wound.

00:35:24.115 --> 00:35:25.207
You're looking well.

00:35:25.249 --> 00:35:26.477
Go!

00:35:26.517 --> 00:35:28.246
I'm not going to leave you.

00:35:31.622 --> 00:35:33.419
It was a pleasure treating you.

00:35:33.458 --> 00:35:35.221
Don't hesitate to call again.

00:35:39.630 --> 00:35:41.257
Are you all right, Mr. Paris?

00:35:41.299 --> 00:35:42.266
Oh, just great.

00:35:42.300 --> 00:35:44.131
Maybe we can go
to the Mess Hall now,

00:35:44.168 --> 00:35:47.501
and let the holographic Neelix
burn my arm with a frying pan.

00:35:47.538 --> 00:35:49.733
Your feeble attempt at wit
notwithstanding,

00:35:49.774 --> 00:35:51.969
it does appear that Seska
has reprogrammed

00:35:52.076 --> 00:35:53.976
the holographic crew
to torture us.

00:35:54.011 --> 00:35:56.343
I suggest we avoid
meeting any more of them.

00:35:56.380 --> 00:35:57.972
Seska to Tuvok.

00:35:58.082 --> 00:36:00.516
I know you can hear me.

00:36:00.551 --> 00:36:02.041
Oh, terrific.

00:36:02.086 --> 00:36:04.384
I just wanted to remind you

00:36:04.422 --> 00:36:07.050
that wherever you go,
I'll find you.

00:36:07.091 --> 00:36:09.025
I say we try
the Jefferies tubes.

00:36:09.060 --> 00:36:11.427
I concur.

00:36:17.332 --> 00:36:18.799
Captain, you're not
going to believe this,

00:36:18.834 --> 00:36:21.234
but Seska caused
these cascade failures.

00:36:21.270 --> 00:36:22.931
Seska? How?

00:36:23.038 --> 00:36:26.201
What she lacked in loyalty,
she made up for in ingenuity.

00:36:26.241 --> 00:36:28.232
According to the backup
computer logs,

00:36:28.277 --> 00:36:31.713
she got into Tuvok's
scenario on stardate 48671,

00:36:31.747 --> 00:36:33.578
about a month
before she left the ship.

00:36:33.615 --> 00:36:35.310
She programmed it
to cause all of these

00:36:35.350 --> 00:36:36.647
shutdowns the next
time Tuvok reopened

00:36:36.685 --> 00:36:40.951
the narrative parameters file,
which he didn't do until today.

00:36:40.989 --> 00:36:42.217
Can we get them out?

00:36:42.257 --> 00:36:46.057
Seska laid booby-trapped
subroutines everywhere.

00:36:46.094 --> 00:36:47.755
If we try to open
the holodeck doors,

00:36:47.796 --> 00:36:50.458
the power grid
is rigged to explode.

00:36:50.499 --> 00:36:51.830
And the transporters
are still off-line.

00:36:51.867 --> 00:36:55.667
You said the narrative
parameters file is open now.

00:36:55.704 --> 00:36:58.571
Seska's revised program
is playing out as we speak.

00:37:01.543 --> 00:37:04.011
If Seska can rewrite Tuvok...

00:37:05.447 --> 00:37:08.780
maybe I can rewrite Seska.

00:37:08.817 --> 00:37:14.414
So, Tuvok, anything
in the "Dictates of Poetics"

00:37:14.456 --> 00:37:15.718
about how to escape

00:37:15.757 --> 00:37:18.225
from a ship
full of insane holograms?

00:37:18.260 --> 00:37:19.352
Your attempts at humor

00:37:19.394 --> 00:37:21.191
are hardly constructive,
Mr. Paris.

00:37:30.472 --> 00:37:32.269
The controls are jammed.

00:37:32.307 --> 00:37:33.535
I cannot close the hatch.

00:37:35.310 --> 00:37:36.709
Tuvok!

00:37:51.260 --> 00:37:53.285
Where do you suppose
this came from?

00:37:53.328 --> 00:37:55.057
That is an intriguing question.

00:37:55.097 --> 00:37:57.258
You think Seska's
toying with us?

00:37:57.299 --> 00:37:59.494
Taking us to the brink
of death again,

00:37:59.535 --> 00:38:00.832
then letting us live,

00:38:00.869 --> 00:38:02.336
so she can keep torturing us?

00:38:02.371 --> 00:38:04.498
I prefer a more optimistic
interpretation.

00:38:04.540 --> 00:38:06.701
It is possible our shipmates
outside the holodeck

00:38:06.742 --> 00:38:08.801
have learned of our predicament

00:38:08.844 --> 00:38:10.175
and have found a way to help us

00:38:10.212 --> 00:38:11.702
by making additions
to the program,

00:38:11.747 --> 00:38:13.476
such as that plasma
extinguisher.

00:38:13.515 --> 00:38:15.574
If you want to look
on the bright side,

00:38:15.617 --> 00:38:17.983
I'm certainly not going
to argue with you.

00:38:25.761 --> 00:38:27.558
If they do know
what's going on,

00:38:27.596 --> 00:38:29.894
why just hand us
a plasma extinguisher?

00:38:29.932 --> 00:38:33.299
Why not shut down the hologrid
or change the scenario?

00:38:33.335 --> 00:38:36.031
I would imagine Seska
has made it very difficult

00:38:36.071 --> 00:38:38.938
for anyone to implement
more than minor changes.

00:38:38.974 --> 00:38:40.373
Take a look at this.

00:38:46.949 --> 00:38:48.507
You were right.

00:38:48.550 --> 00:38:50.848
We must follow
their instructions.

00:38:55.223 --> 00:38:56.190
Hello, boys.

00:38:56.224 --> 00:38:59.785
What do you say we go
for a little walk?

00:39:02.698 --> 00:39:04.859
Where did they come from?

00:39:07.436 --> 00:39:09.666
Seska's program is
adding new algorithms

00:39:09.705 --> 00:39:11.229
to counteract
the changes we're making.

00:39:11.273 --> 00:39:12.900
I need more access
to the narrative subroutines.

00:39:12.941 --> 00:39:14.306
I can't get in.

00:39:14.343 --> 00:39:16.277
You better find a way.

00:39:16.311 --> 00:39:17.903
Otherwise, Tom and Tuvok
aren't going to make it

00:39:17.946 --> 00:39:19.140
out of there alive.

00:39:25.253 --> 00:39:26.880
It looks like
Chakotay's taking them

00:39:26.922 --> 00:39:28.549
to the holographic cargo bay.

00:39:28.590 --> 00:39:30.080
Torres to Kim.
How are you coming

00:39:30.125 --> 00:39:31.092
with those transporters?

00:39:31.126 --> 00:39:32.923
Seska's program
has completely disabled

00:39:32.961 --> 00:39:34.622
the relay access ports.

00:39:34.663 --> 00:39:37.097
It's going to take a while to
get Tom and Tuvok out of there.

00:39:37.132 --> 00:39:38.963
I guess that means
I keep writing.

00:39:40.402 --> 00:39:41.699
As you can see,

00:39:41.737 --> 00:39:43.261
the last of your comrades
have been captured.

00:39:43.305 --> 00:39:46.035
In case anybody had any doubts,
it should be obvious by now

00:39:46.074 --> 00:39:48.133
that this is no longer
a Starfleet vessel.

00:39:48.176 --> 00:39:51.703
Bring Paris and Tuvok over here.

00:39:51.747 --> 00:39:53.908
You and you, bring your weapons.

00:39:57.986 --> 00:39:58.953
What are you doing?

00:39:59.021 --> 00:40:00.215
What do you think I'm doing?

00:40:00.255 --> 00:40:02.280
I'm going to execute them
right here, right now.

00:40:02.324 --> 00:40:05.054
I need access to
the character algorithms now.

00:40:05.093 --> 00:40:06.060
I'm on it.

00:40:06.094 --> 00:40:07.391
Fire on my order.

00:40:07.429 --> 00:40:08.726
Belay that.

00:40:08.764 --> 00:40:11.528
What are you doing?
We planned this.

00:40:11.566 --> 00:40:14.091
I'm not sure it's necessary
to kill them.

00:40:14.136 --> 00:40:16.229
If I'm not mistaken,
the Chakotay hologram

00:40:16.271 --> 00:40:18.432
is undergoing some sort
of character change.

00:40:18.473 --> 00:40:20.338
Do you think they're trying
to help us again?

00:40:20.375 --> 00:40:21.569
These two rodents betrayed us.

00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:22.599
They deserve to die.

00:40:22.644 --> 00:40:23.975
Don't listen to her, Commander.

00:40:24.012 --> 00:40:25.741
You've taken the ship.

00:40:25.781 --> 00:40:27.840
There is no need to add murder
to your list of offenses.

00:40:27.883 --> 00:40:29.578
Quiet!

00:40:29.618 --> 00:40:31.245
Lower your weapons.

00:40:31.286 --> 00:40:32.583
It's working.

00:40:32.621 --> 00:40:34.589
Now, if I can
just keep modifying

00:40:34.623 --> 00:40:36.090
the Chakotay hologram...

00:40:36.124 --> 00:40:39.355
You're not going
to lose your nerve, are you?

00:40:39.394 --> 00:40:40.691
We have what we want.

00:40:40.729 --> 00:40:42.458
There's no reason to kill them.

00:40:42.497 --> 00:40:45.193
Prepare to fire on my order!

00:40:45.233 --> 00:40:48.964
Seska, I'm in command
of this operation.

00:40:49.004 --> 00:40:50.471
Not anymore!

00:40:52.908 --> 00:40:54.876
I don't believe it.

00:40:54.910 --> 00:40:57.879
The program is reconfiguring
the sub-processors

00:40:57.913 --> 00:40:59.881
to counter every change we make.

00:40:59.915 --> 00:41:02.543
No matter what we do,
it rewrites itself

00:41:02.584 --> 00:41:05.212
so that Tom and Tuvok
will die.

00:41:05.253 --> 00:41:07.949
I'm not out of ideas yet.

00:41:08.023 --> 00:41:11.288
Is there anyone else who wants
to challenge my authority?

00:41:14.596 --> 00:41:17.064
Isn't their loyalty inspiring?

00:41:17.099 --> 00:41:19.966
Set your phasers to "kill."

00:41:20.035 --> 00:41:21.366
Don't listen to her.

00:41:21.403 --> 00:41:23.268
Fire on my order.

00:41:25.207 --> 00:41:27.198
What the hell was that?

00:41:35.817 --> 00:41:37.307
Don't move, Seska.

00:41:37.352 --> 00:41:39.752
Bridge to Seska.

00:41:39.788 --> 00:41:42.086
We're under attack
by the Rukani.

00:41:42.124 --> 00:41:43.819
The Rukani?!

00:41:43.859 --> 00:41:45.759
The people the Captain
and I were visiting

00:41:45.794 --> 00:41:47.318
while you were busy
taking over the ship.

00:41:47.362 --> 00:41:49.830
When we realized there
was a mutiny in progress,

00:41:49.865 --> 00:41:51.856
we called them
for a little assistance.

00:41:51.900 --> 00:41:53.868
Harry, have you got
transporters yet?

00:41:53.902 --> 00:41:55.927
Still working on it, Captain.

00:41:55.971 --> 00:41:57.962
You're not getting
this ship back.

00:41:58.006 --> 00:42:00.440
That is a rather bold statement
for someone in your position.

00:42:00.475 --> 00:42:03.376
Computer, initiate 60-second
self-destruct sequence.

00:42:03.411 --> 00:42:04.844
Authorization: Zeta-one.

00:42:04.880 --> 00:42:08.213
This ship will self-destruct
in 60 seconds.

00:42:08.250 --> 00:42:09.717
Computer, belay that order.

00:42:09.751 --> 00:42:12.083
Authorization:
Tuvok-four-seven-seven-four.

00:42:12.120 --> 00:42:13.610
Unable to comply.

00:42:13.655 --> 00:42:15.054
Voiceprint not recognized.

00:42:15.090 --> 00:42:17.388
If you don't
hand over that phaser rifle,

00:42:17.425 --> 00:42:19.222
everyone on this ship
is going to be dead in...

00:42:19.261 --> 00:42:22.059
Self-destruct in 45 seconds.

00:42:22.097 --> 00:42:24.065
I don't know how she rigged it,
Captain,

00:42:24.099 --> 00:42:25.726
but when she ordered
the self-destruct,

00:42:25.767 --> 00:42:28.395
it initiated an overload
in the holodeck power relays.

00:42:28.436 --> 00:42:30.233
The whole grid is going to blow.

00:42:31.640 --> 00:42:33.198
Self-destruct in 30 seconds.

00:42:33.241 --> 00:42:36.472
Hand over the weapon,
or the ship is going

00:42:36.511 --> 00:42:38.069
to be destroyed.

00:42:38.113 --> 00:42:40.240
I have set this phaser to kill.

00:42:40.282 --> 00:42:43.251
If you do not deactivate
the self-destruct sequence,

00:42:43.285 --> 00:42:44.616
I will fire.

00:42:44.653 --> 00:42:46.518
I'm surprised at you, Tuvok.

00:42:46.555 --> 00:42:47.988
That's not very logical.

00:42:48.056 --> 00:42:51.389
If I'm dead, who'll turn off
the self-destruct?

00:42:51.426 --> 00:42:53.860
15 seconds to self-destruct.

00:42:53.895 --> 00:42:57.729
13... 12... 11...

00:42:57.766 --> 00:42:58.733
ten... nine...

00:42:58.767 --> 00:42:59.995
Computer...

00:43:00.101 --> 00:43:02.661
terminate
self-destruct sequence.

00:43:02.704 --> 00:43:04.171
Authorization: Zeta-one.

00:43:04.206 --> 00:43:07.073
Self-destruct sequence
has been terminated.

00:43:07.108 --> 00:43:09.338
Now call off
your Rukani friends.

00:43:09.377 --> 00:43:10.708
Do what she says.

00:43:10.745 --> 00:43:12.212
Tuvok...

00:43:12.247 --> 00:43:13.805
That's an order, Mr. Paris.

00:43:17.919 --> 00:43:20.888
Paris to the Rukani vessel.

00:43:20.922 --> 00:43:22.719
Thank you for your assistance,

00:43:22.757 --> 00:43:24.952
but everything's
under control now.

00:43:24.993 --> 00:43:26.290
It is, isn't it?

00:43:26.328 --> 00:43:28.262
I guess, if you want
something done right,

00:43:28.296 --> 00:43:31.265
you've got to do it yourself.

00:43:37.606 --> 00:43:39.574
Not bad.

00:43:39.608 --> 00:43:41.235
Seska's not the only one

00:43:41.276 --> 00:43:43.938
who knows how to cause
a phaser malfunction.

00:43:45.881 --> 00:43:49.373
The holographic simulation
has ended.

00:43:51.253 --> 00:43:52.686
It's over.

00:43:52.721 --> 00:43:53.983
Kim to Engineering.

00:43:54.055 --> 00:43:55.989
I think I can give you
transporters now, Captain.

00:43:56.024 --> 00:43:58.117
That's all right, Harry.

00:43:58.159 --> 00:43:59.922
No rush.

00:44:08.937 --> 00:44:11.030
Here's to stories
with happy endings.

00:44:13.675 --> 00:44:14.937
I must say, Captain,

00:44:15.010 --> 00:44:17.035
causing the alien ship
to come to our aid

00:44:17.078 --> 00:44:18.943
was a very effective
plot development.

00:44:19.047 --> 00:44:21.880
Who says deus ex machina
is an outdated literary device?

00:44:21.917 --> 00:44:23.316
I'm just glad

00:44:23.351 --> 00:44:25.148
you didn't come down
with a case of writer's block.

00:44:25.186 --> 00:44:27.848
So, you two are going
to have to come up

00:44:27.889 --> 00:44:31.552
with a new idea for your
next literary collaboration.

00:44:31.593 --> 00:44:33.185
What about doing a Western?

00:44:33.228 --> 00:44:34.855
Or a detective story.

00:44:34.896 --> 00:44:36.488
I don't care
what kind of story it is,

00:44:36.531 --> 00:44:38.294
as long as I'm not
the bad guy this time.

00:44:40.635 --> 00:44:43.229
I've got a great idea
for a holonovel

00:44:43.271 --> 00:44:46.069
about a daring trader
who becomes a cook

00:44:46.107 --> 00:44:47.074
on a starship.

00:44:47.108 --> 00:44:48.075
Eventually, he rises...

00:44:48.109 --> 00:44:50.669
Mr. Neelix, if Mr. Paris and I

00:44:50.712 --> 00:44:52.907
do create another work
of holofiction,

00:44:52.948 --> 00:44:54.973
I assure you,
we will choose a subject

00:44:55.050 --> 00:44:56.950
much less close to home.
